            <div xml:id="d199">

                <pb facs="0381" n="291" sameAs="frus:frus1932v02/pg291"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.00/2713: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany (Sackett) to the Acting Secretary
                            of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-04-14T19:00:00+01:00">April 14, 1932—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 14—3:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>76. My 75, April 14, 10 a.m. Hitler in
                    interview today declared to American journalists that disbanding of his military
                    organizations <pb facs="0382" n="292" xml:id="pg292"/> by government was in
                    response to pressure exerted by Tardieu.
                    Foreign Office has privately but earnestly requested that Department be notified
                    that this allegation lacks any vestige of truth.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Sackett</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
